7. Your entire playbook flow

Your first run, when Docker wasn't installed, was:

Check Docker
     ↓
Docker not found
     ↓
failed = true
     ↓
ignore_errors
     ↓
Install Docker

Now you ran it again:

Check Docker
     ↓
Docker found
     ↓
failed = false
     ↓
when: output.failed = false
     ↓
Skip Docker installation

That's exactly how conditional error handling works.

7. Understand main output

server1 : ok=3 changed=1 unreachable=0 failed=0 skipped=1 rescued=0 ignored=0

Meaning:

| Value           | Meaning                          |
| --------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `ok=3`          | 3 tasks completed successfully   |
| `changed=1`     | 1 task made a change             |
| `unreachable=0` | Server connection was successful |
| `failed=0`      | No task failed                   |
| `skipped=1`     | 1 task was skipped               |
| `ignored=0`     | No errors were ignored this time |

The skipped=1 is your:

Install Docker if it is not installed

task.

